# SEED lock-in

## The mechanism

`src/app/styles/global.css` runs `@theme { --*: initial; }` after importing Tailwind, which deletes
every built-in Tailwind design token. It then imports `@seed-design/tailwind4-theme`, which
re-populates the theme with SEED's tokens and redefines `p-*`, `m-*`, `w-*`, `h-*`, `size-*` and
`gap-*` to accept SEED dimensions only.

The consequence you must internalise: **a non-SEED utility is not an error, it is a no-op.**
`bg-red-500`, `p-4`, `text-lg`, `rounded-md`, `shadow-md` and `max-w-3xl` all compile to nothing and
the element simply renders unstyled. The `seed-lockin/token-only` ESLint rule exists to turn that
silence into a message; do not disable it.

## Writing a className

| You want      | You write                                                 | Never               |
| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- |
| Background    | `bg-bg-layer-default`, `bg-bg-brand-solid`                | `bg-white`          |
| Text colour   | `text-fg-neutral`, `text-fg-neutral-muted`                | `text-gray-500`     |
| Border colour | `border-stroke-neutral-muted`                             | `border-gray-200`   |
| Spacing       | `p-x4`, `px-x5`, `gap-x3`, `mt-x2`                        | `p-4`, `gap-2`      |
| Position      | `top-x2`, `inset-x0`                                      | `top-4`             |
| Radius        | `rounded-r4`, `rounded-full`                              | `rounded-lg`        |
| Shadow        | `shadow-s1`, `shadow-s2`                                  | `shadow-md`         |
| Text style    | `t4-bold`, `t7-regular`, `screen-title`, `article-body`   | `text-lg font-bold` |
| Breakpoint    | `sm:` 480, `md:` 768, `lg:` 1280, `xl:` 1440 (SEED scale) | —                   |

Typography is one class, not a composition: use `t5-bold`, not `text-size-t5 font-bold`.

**The text scale counts upwards.** `t1` is 11px and `t14` is 48px, which is the opposite of the
heading conventions most CSS frameworks use. Body copy sits around `t4` (14px) or `t5` (16px);
captions at `t2`–`t3`; a section heading at `t6`–`t7`. For a screen title prefer the named
`screen-title` (t10, bold), and for long-form prose `article-body` (t5, regular). Getting this
backwards produces a page that renders but reads inside out, so check the scale rather than
assuming.

The full list of valid tokens for the installed version lives in
`.cursor/rules/_generated-seed-tokens.mdc` and `.seed/tokens.json`. When you are unsure, call
`get_rootage` or `get_react_component` on the `seed-docs` MCP server rather than guessing.

## Components

Import SEED components from `seed-design/ui/*`, which maps to `src/shared/seed/ui/`:

```tsx
import { ActionButton } from "seed-design/ui/action-button";
import { TextField, TextFieldInput } from "seed-design/ui/text-field";
```

These files are snippets fetched by `@seed-design/cli`. If the component you need is missing, add it
with `pnpm seed:add ui:<name>` instead of hand-rolling one. Only `src/shared/seed/**` and
`src/shared/ui/**` may import `@seed-design/react` directly.

Icons come from `@karrotmarket/react-monochrome-icon` and `@karrotmarket/react-multicolor-icon`. Find
the right one with `search_icons` on the MCP server; it understands Korean queries.

## Escape hatches

There are two, and both are deliberate friction:

- An inline `style` attribute needs a `// seed-escape: <reason>` comment directly above it.
- A genuinely missing token goes into the project `@theme` block in `src/app/styles/global.css`,
  with a comment explaining why SEED has no equivalent. Today that block holds only the breakpoints,
  the Pretendard font stack and one content width.

Reach for these rarely. If you find yourself wanting a third one, the design is probably fighting
the design system.
